<h1>Pharmaceutical &amp; Cleanroom Conveyors</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">Pharmaceutical conveyors transport tablets, capsules, vials, syringes, and packaging components through cleanroom environments while meeting ISO 14644 classification requirements and cGMP (current Good Manufacturing Practice) regulations. These systems use 316L stainless steel frames, enclosed belt housings with HEPA filtration, low-particulate drive components, and validated material documentation. Containment conveyors add isolator integration and HEPA-filtered exhaust for handling highly potent compounds (HPAPIs). Manufacturers like Dorner, mk North America, Bosch Rexroth, FlexLink, and NCC Automated Systems supply pharmaceutical-grade conveyor platforms.</p>
<h2 id="iso-heading">ISO Cleanroom Classifications</h2>
<p><a href="https://www.iso.org/standard/53394.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ISO 14644-1</a> defines cleanroom classifications by the maximum allowable particle count per cubic meter of air. Each classification imposes specific requirements on the conveyor equipment operating within that space. The conveyor itself must not generate particles that would violate the room classification, every moving part, belt surface, and lubricated joint is a potential particle source.</p>
